  "term": "ranked data",
  "definition": "Ranked data are observations organized by their position in an ordered list, such as from largest to smallest. In this form, the main focus is the relationship between a value and its rank, which can produce patterns such as power-law, exponential, Gaussian, or Zipf-like distributions.",
